  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 200 PM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nNorthwesterly flow aloft is forecast to continue through the\nupcoming week. A storm system is forecast to pass to our north \nand east Tuesday night through Wednesday night with 20 to 30 \npercent chances of showers and storms. Models show a slight \nincrease in moisture ahead of this storm system. Currently the \nhigher chances of precipitation are across northwest Illinois. \nRainfall amounts will be light with generally less than a tenth \nof an inch expected. High temperatures on Wednesday will be \nslightly warmer into the lower to mid 80s.\n\nAfter Wednesday night, models show another shortwave topping \nthe western U.S. ridge and flattening the flow aloft to more \nzonal. This system will begin to impact the area late Friday \nnight into Saturday, bringing more humid conditions and another\nchance for precipitation.",
